# Pinned component versions, in one file, sourced by the install scripts.
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT INLINE DEFAULTS: the previous project lost an evening to
# an unpinned Helm chart. The External Secrets chart moved from 1.x to 2.x
# between two runs, 2.x dropped the v1beta1 API the manifests used, and the
# error — "no matches for kind ExternalSecret" — named the manifests rather
# than the chart that had changed under them.
#
# It happened again while building THIS project, in a worse form. See the note
# at the bottom of falco/values.yaml: the Falco chart replaced a configuration
# key between 4.x and 9.x, the chart ships no values schema, and Helm accepts
# unknown keys SILENTLY. The install succeeded, Falco ran, and the setting had
# no effect. Nothing reported it.
#
# Every value here is overridable from the environment, so a version bump is
# testable without editing the repository:
#
#   KYVERNO_CHART_VERSION=3.8.2 ./scripts/01-install-policy-engines.sh
#
# WHEN A PIN IS WRONG the install script says so and prints the available
# versions rather than falling back to latest. A silent fallback to latest is
# how you end up running something you did not choose.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kyverno — chart 3.9.1 maps to Kyverno 1.19.1.
#
# The policies in policies/kyverno/ are `kyverno.io/v1 ClusterPolicy` objects,
# one of which uses a `verifyImages` rule. Kyverno 1.19 PRINTS A DEPRECATION
# WARNING for that API:
#
#   Warning: kyverno.io/v1 ClusterPolicy is deprecated and will be removed in
#   a future release; migrate to ValidatingPolicy, MutatingPolicy,
#   GeneratingPolicy or ImageValidatingPolicy (policies.kyverno.io)
#
# It is a warning, not a removal, and the policies were verified working on
# exactly this version:
#
#   kyverno test policies/kyverno/tests          24/24 passed
#   kyverno apply policies/kyverno/01-...yaml    reached ghcr.io and refused
#                                                an unsigned digest correctly
#
# Pinned here rather than left to float BECAUSE of that warning. When the API
# is eventually removed, an unpinned install would stop enforcing on a cluster
# whose manifests had not changed — and `kubectl get clusterpolicy` would
# still list all five. The migration path is named above; take it deliberately,
# not by being upgraded into it.
#
# 01-install-policy-engines.sh asserts after install that the CRD really does
# accept a verifyImages rule, rather than trusting that the chart version
# implies it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
: "${KYVERNO_CHART_VERSION:=3.9.1}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Falco — chart 9.2.0 maps to Falco 0.45.0.
#
# falco/values.yaml is written against THIS schema and was verified by
# rendering the chart with it. Chart 4.x and 9.x configure the container
# runtime socket differently and the older spelling is silently ignored by the
# newer chart, so this pin and that file have to move together.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
: "${FALCO_CHART_VERSION:=9.2.0}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Istio. Pinned because the sidecar image tag falls inside the blast radius of
# the Kyverno registry allowlist: an Istio upgrade changes the injected image,
# and a mismatch there rejects every pod in the mesh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
: "${ISTIO_VERSION:=1.26.2}"

# ArgoCD is installed from its released manifest rather than a chart, so this
# is a git tag on the argo-cd repository. `stable` is a moving target; this is
# not.
: "${ARGOCD_VERSION:=v2.13.2}"

# cosign on the BOX, used by scripts/04-verify-signature-identity.sh to verify
# the same signature Kyverno verifies, by hand. Matches the version the CI
# workflow pins, so a difference in behaviour between the two cannot be a
# version difference.
: "${COSIGN_VERSION:=v2.4.1}"

export KYVERNO_CHART_VERSION FALCO_CHART_VERSION ISTIO_VERSION \
       ARGOCD_VERSION COSIGN_VERSION
